        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What exactly is kapok fiber?",
            "answer": "<p>Kapok is a natural fiber harvested from the seed pods of the kapok tree, native to Southeast Asia. Unlike cotton, no tree cutting is required — the pods simply fall and the fluff is collected. The fiber is hollow, making it naturally lightweight and thermally efficient. KAPOK KNOT has developed a process to transform this fiber into a high-performance insulation sheet called EthicalDown Kapok™.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it machine washable?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Unlike down jackets that require dry cleaning, the AirLight Jacket can be machine washed on a gentle, cold-water cycle. Kapok fiber does not clump or degrade with repeated washing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is your shipping and return policy?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Shipping:</strong> Free worldwide shipping on the first 100 launch orders (standard rate applies afterwards). Orders are dispatched from Japan within 3–5 business days; international delivery typically takes 7–14 days.</p><p><strong>Returns:</strong> As a special launch-edition offer at 20% off, we are unable to accept change-of-mind returns on launch orders. If your item arrives faulty, damaged or not as described, we will replace or refund it at our cost — this always applies, including your rights under the Australian Consumer Law. Questions about sizing before you order? Email service@kapok-knot.com — we respond within 2 business days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does sizing work?",
            "answer": "<p>The AirLight Jacket is designed with a relaxed, slightly oversized fit. If you prefer a fitted look, we recommend sizing down. Detailed size charts are available on the product page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is KAPOK KNOT really sustainable?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, on multiple levels. Kapok requires no irrigation, no pesticides, and no tree cutting. Our founder personally maintains direct contracts with farms and processing facilities in Southeast Asia. Increased kapok demand also drives reforestation in the region.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_duties": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I have to pay customs duties or import taxes?",
            "answer": "<p>Depending on your country, customs duties and import taxes may be charged when your parcel arrives — these are set by your local customs authority and are not included in our prices. As a guide: the US applies duties on apparel imports, the EU applies VAT plus duty above €150, and Australia applies 10% GST. We mark all parcels accurately and are working to bring duty-inclusive checkout to our store.</p>"
          }
        }
